<% content_for :title, "Privacy Policy | FamilyPlates" %>

<%= render layout: "legal/document", locals: { title: "Privacy Policy" } do %>
  <p>
    Draft. Not in effect. Stasis State LLC is a proposed name and has not been formed. This
    page is not a contract with that company. Do not pay, and do not treat signup as acceptance
    of a contract with that company, until this draft notice is removed and the operator is
    named without this notice.
  </p>

  <p>
    This policy explains what the hosted FamilyPlates service (the "Service"), operated by
    [DRAFT TARGET, NOT FORMED: Stasis State LLC] ("we", "us"), collects, why, and the choices you have. The Service
    is offered only in the United States.
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Account information:</strong> your email address, and the household and profile names you enter.</li>
    <li><strong>Household content:</strong> recipes, meal plans, grocery lists, pantry items, notes, cook assignments, profile colors and icons, and your household's time zone.</li>
    <li><strong>Security data:</strong> hashed profile PINs, passkey public keys, and records of signed-in sessions and paired devices.</li>
    <li><strong>Billing information:</strong> your plan, subscription status, and payment history. Stripe collects your card details. We never see or store your full card number.</li>
    <li><strong>Support messages</strong> you send us.</li>
    <li><strong>Technical data:</strong> IP address and request logs, used for security, abuse prevention, and troubleshooting.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    An adult Organizer may add profiles for children in the household. A profile holds only
    what the Organizer enters, such as a first name, an avatar, and meal assignments. We do not
    knowingly collect personal information directly from children under 13. Children's profiles
    have no email address or account of their own. If you believe a child has given us personal
    information, contact us and we will delete it.
  </p>

  <h2>How we use it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>to provide the Service: planning, grocery lists, calendar feeds, printouts, and sync across your devices;</li>
    <li>to sign you in and keep your account secure;</li>
    <li>to bill your subscription;</li>
    <li>to answer support requests and send service emails, such as sign-in codes;</li>
    <li>to comply with the law and enforce our <%= link_to "Terms of Service", terms_path %>.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    <strong>We do not sell or share your personal information</strong> for cross-context
    behavioral advertising. We do not use third-party advertising or analytics trackers.
  </p>

  <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
  <p>We share data only with service providers who process it on our behalf:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Stripe</strong>, for payments and subscription management;</li>
    <li><strong>[EMAIL PROVIDER]</strong>, to deliver sign-in codes and service email;</li>
    <li><strong>[HOSTING PROVIDER]</strong>, which hosts our servers and backups.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We may also disclose information if the law requires it, or to protect the safety of
    users or the Service. Our operators may view household information when needed for
    support, billing, or security, and that access is logged.
  </p>

  <h2>Third-party content</h2>
  <p>
    Recipe images can come from other websites, such as the page a recipe was imported from.
    Your browser loads those images directly from those sites, which can see your IP address.
    When you import a recipe, our servers fetch the page, not your browser.
  </p>

  <h2>Cookies and local storage</h2>
  <p>We use only what the Service needs to work. There are no advertising or analytics cookies.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Session cookies</strong> keep you signed in, remember the active household profile, and protect forms against cross-site request forgery.</li>
    <li><strong>Browser local storage</strong> remembers your light or dark theme, grocery checklist ticks, and your place in Cook Mode, on that device only.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Stripe sets its own cookies on its checkout and billing pages, under
    <a href="https://stripe.com/privacy" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Stripe's privacy policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>
    We keep household data while your account is active. When a deletion request is completed,
    we delete your household's data from our live systems. Copies in backups are removed as the
    backups expire, within [BACKUP RETENTION PERIOD]. We keep billing records as long as tax and
    accounting law requires.
  </p>

  <h2>Your choices and rights</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Access and export:</strong> download your household's data at any time from the account data page.</li>
    <li><strong>Correction:</strong> edit your information in the app, or ask us.</li>
    <li><strong>Deletion:</strong> request deletion of your household from the account data page, or by contacting us.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Depending on your state (for example, California), you may have more rights, including the
    right to know what we collect and the right not to be discriminated against for using your
    rights. To make a request, use in-app support or email [CONTACT EMAIL]. We may need to
    verify your identity first.
  </p>

  <h2>Security</h2>
  <p>
    Data is encrypted in transit with TLS. Session tokens, PINs, and passwords are stored
    hashed. No system is perfectly secure. If a breach affects your
    information, we will notify you as the law requires.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    If we change this policy materially, we will notify you before the change takes effect.
    The effective date above shows when it last changed.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>[DRAFT TARGET, NOT FORMED: Stasis State LLC], [MAILING ADDRESS], [CONTACT EMAIL].</p>
<% end %>
